      "id": "minimax-h3-fasth3-omni-tts-r2v",
      "name": "MiniMax H3 Emotion TTS Lip-Sync (FastH3 Omni)",
      "icon": "🗣",
      "description": "Type a line, pick the mood, and supply a voice sample and a picture. IndexTTS 2.5 speaks the line in that voice and FastH3 Omni lip-syncs the character to it, in one generation.\n\nPick this over the Emotion TTS Lip-Sync v2 card for speed and a closer match to your picture. It was about 20% faster on a 12 GB card (105-108 s against 133-137 s per 6 s shot at 480p, voice clone included) and just as accurate: a 7 word line came out word for word on 3 of 3 seeds, then silence. In an angry-line test the v2 card tinted the hair red on all three seeds and once pulled the microphone from the reference photo into the shot. This card did neither.\n\nSparse attention (More Advanced Options, on by default) is where the speed comes from. Switched off, the same shot takes about 150 s and comes out somewhat different on the same seed. Faster Attention (Sage) is not used on this card.\n\nHow to use it:\n\n1. Audio slot: a voice sample, 3-10 s of clean speech. It is cloned, not lip-synced, and the line is spoken in English.\n\n2. Reference images: the character(s), up to nine.\n\n3. Prompt: a normal H3 shot description with the line in double quotes. Describe the lips closing after the line and what happens for the rest of the shot.\n\n4. Emotion (optional): an [emotion: ...] tag, e.g. [emotion: angry, clipped].\n\n5. Duration: fit it to the line (IndexTTS speaks about 3-5 words a second). A line too long for the shot gets rushed or cut off at the start.\n\nBefore installing: this needs the v0.42.0 engine. It downloads the 22.2 GB FastH3 Omni checkpoint (shared with the FastH3 Omni pack) plus 7.7 GB of IndexTTS 2.5 weights. The IndexTTS node downgrades the engine's transformers (5.x to 4.57.x); SimpliGen's maintainer has confirmed this is allowed and it sticks across engine updates. If the IndexTTS node cannot find its weights on the first run, restart SimpliGen once.",
      "tagline": "Cloned-voice lip-sync on FastH3 Omni: about 20% faster, closer to your picture",
